{"title":"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axes and externally tangent to the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af424ab2c41e93a9e7ab081dee423809b2ba735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the sum of all possible radii of the circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c636728460bb7e2dfea229a64f8705023390f8f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of our circle. For it to be tangent to the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axes, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a72eda99c2e130d05a4d80be9b85f2fa0460ae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=(r,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />. For the circle to be externally tangent to the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af424ab2c41e93a9e7ab081dee423809b2ba735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af424ab2c41e93a9e7ab081dee423809b2ba735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> must be exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/080bdd4b53cf3c5d997f0ee91d272b451f0827d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a> the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a76bb04cc1ad44439278c1c3e84ee59386dff41f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af424ab2c41e93a9e7ab081dee423809b2ba735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b5e69f80156b6e186ac0d57ce541bc70182c3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{ (r-3)^2 + r^2 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"120\" height=\"35\" />, hence we get the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa88b75f8bd2aa6bcc3e28d1a85a3cb242f22c59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-3)^2 + r^2 = (r+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Simplifying, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/6720be6ba31893c0dcc2b9382167dc73c7009876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2 - 8r + 8 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" />. By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s formulas\">Vieta's formulas</a> the sum of the two roots of this equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81ca9c5c8715be868438500743202d6773d05bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>(We should actually solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to verify that there are two distinct positive roots. In this case we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c890370c352c3013e8f5d42ae72a3a3438dd3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=4\\pm 2\\sqrt 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />. This is generally a good rule of thumb, but is not necessary as all of the available answers are integers, and the equation obviously doesn't factor as integers. You can also tell that there are two positive roots based on the visual interpretation.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f9e3359dbc3787009e504d0ccc9d485a3c74ef1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); defaultpen(0.8); filldraw( Circle( (3,0), 1 ), lightgray, black ); draw( (0,0) -- (15,0), Arrow ); draw( (0,0) -- (0,15), Arrow ); draw( (0,0) -- (15,15), dashed ); real r1 = 4 - 2*sqrt(2), r2 = 4 + 2*sqrt(2); pair S1=(r1,r1), S2=(r2,r2); dot(S1); dot(S2); dot((3,0)); draw( Circle(S1,r1) ); draw( Circle(S2,r2) ); [/asy]\" width=\"362\" height=\"382\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A\">2009 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;